  "anti_overclaim": "No cycle of any length is excluded or claimed in either problem. The Collatz numbers are re-derived from a classical inequality, not new; Barina's 2025 bound needs a sharper averaging than this inequality. The Juggler 1-cycle length 9809721694 survives finance at N_0 = 3.5e8, which records that no Juggler analogue of Steiner's theorem exists, not that a cycle does."
